          "english_quote": "The place was steep and cut off by the waters.",
          "issue": "“Cut off by the waters” describes isolation or blocked access rather than the terrain's being broken or rent by water. It adds that spatial implication while losing the source's description of the ground's physical condition.",
          "suggested_revision": "Proposed for fresh review: “The place was steep and broken up by the waters.” Preserve the description of water-riven terrain rather than implying that surrounding water isolated the place.",
