          "source_quote": "ἦν δὲ ὁ τόπος κρημνώδης καὶ ἀπερρηγὼς ἀπὸ τῶν ὑδάτων.",
          "english_quote": "The place was steep and cut off by the waters.",
          "issue": "Independently against the Greek, this describes the place as isolated by water instead of describing terrain broken or rent by water. The simplified edition therefore inherits a semantic defect, not merely the standard edition's wording.",
